    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24703" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invectīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		inveho, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>imported</i>, <i>not indigenous</i>,
				<i>not native</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columbae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 29, 41, § 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frumentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Off. 3, 7</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gaudium,</span>”
				i. e. <i>not hearty</i>, <i>not sincere</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 23, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
